EXEC_SUMMARY = [
    "This document sets out the business requirements for the Document Registration module of Kaveri 3.0. It covers the "
    "complete life of a document from the citizen's online pre-registration entry, through scrutiny by the Sub-Registrar, "
    "payment of stamp duty and fees, digital execution (e-Sign / DSC) and appointment booking, to presentation, admission, "
    "photo and thumb capture, endorsement and registration at the Sub-Registrar Office. It also covers the exception paths "
    "that the Registration Act, 1908 and the Karnataka Stamp Act, 1957 provide: delay and condonation, absent executants "
    "(summons and commission), under-valuation references under Sec. 45-A, impounding under Sec. 33, refusal to register, "
    "appeals and applications to the District Registrar, withdrawal before registration and refunds.",
    "The future-state design replaces manual selection and calculation with rule-driven services. The citizen picks the "
    "Transaction Intent and Nature of Document; the system determines the Article of the Schedule, imports property and "
    "owner data from the source-of-truth systems (E-Swathu, BBMP E-Aasthi, E-Aasthi, BDA, KHB, Bhoomi and Mojini), "
    "checks stays, Sec. 22-A prohibited properties and Sec. 22-B stays through a separate microservice, and calculates the "
    "guidance value, stamp duty, surcharge, cess and registration fee through dedicated microservices. Statutory time limits "
    "(4 months for presentation and appearance, condonation windows, 30-day appeal limits, refund limitation periods) are "
    "calculated and enforced by the system rather than tracked on paper.",
    "Each process is described with its To-Be swimlane diagram, a numbered step table, key characteristics and an "
    "application status model, followed by functional requirements, business rules, integrations, a requirements "
    "traceability matrix and non-functional requirements. Statutory references are taken from the Acts, Rules and "
    "notifications held in the Acts_Rules/Document folder; items that depend on documents not held in that folder are "
    "marked for confirmation by the Department.",
]

SCOPE = [
    "Citizen pre-registration entry (online): transaction intent and nature of document, property capture (immovable, movable, "
    "TDR; inside or outside Karnataka; agricultural or non-agricultural), import from source-of-truth systems, parties, "
    "representatives, witnesses, identity verification (Aadhaar e-KYC or manual ID), PAN / Form 97 rule, allotment, "
    "transaction details, Article determination, fee calculation, exemptions, denoting / credit claims, recitals, "
    "covenants, draft deed and submission.",
    "Scrutiny by the Sub-Registrar: verification checklist (common and Article-specific checks), cross-check with the "
    "source of truth, guidance value and fee re-calculation, and the decision to approve for payment, revert or reject.",
    "Payment, digital signing and appointment: full or partial payment (Sec. 45-A under-valuation / Sec. 33 short levy), "
    "Khajane-II / payment gateway, signing list and tracker, e-Sign / DSC by parties and witnesses, deed lock, last date for "
    "presentation, and slot booking at the jurisdictional Sub-Registrar Office.",
    "Presentation and registration at the Sub-Registrar Office: presentation checklist, presenter, admission or denial of "
    "execution, Party Appearance Pending, summons and commission, delay checks and condonation referral, identifiers, "
    "photo, thumb impression, e-KYC and e-Sign capture, endorsement, DSC and registration number generation.",
    "Refusal to register (Part XII, Registration Act; Chapter XXIV, Karnataka Registration Rules): refusal order, partial "
    "registration, Book 2, blocking of re-presentation, refund of half the registration fee and return of the document.",
    "Withdrawal before registration (Rules 23(f), 193(i)) and refunds: registration fee and copying fee refund (Rules "
    "193–195) and stamp duty refund for e-stamp certificates (Karnataka Stamp Act, Sec. 47–51; e-Stamping Rules 31, 32).",
    "District Registrar referrals and appeals: condonation of delay (Sec. 25, 34; Rules 51–55), Sec. 45-A under-valuation "
    "references, Sec. 33 impounded instruments, appeals under Sec. 72 and applications under Sec. 73, and the further "
    "remedies available against the District Registrar's orders.",
    "Shared microservices used by the module: Guidance Value, Stays & Liabilities, Fee Calculation, Deed Generation "
    "(draft deed, final deed, endorsement and registered document from the deed templates), and the Article "
    "determination rules (Decision_Flow).",
    "Integrations: source-of-truth property systems, UIDAI e-KYC, Protean (passport), Income Tax Department (PAN), "
    "e-Sign service provider, DSC certifying authorities, Khajane-II / payment gateway, e-stamp (SHCIL / CRA) database, "
    "SMS / email gateways, DigiLocker and Sakala (if notified).",
    "Bilingual user interface (English and Kannada), notifications, audit trail, role-based access, reports and MIS.",
    "Out of scope for this BRD: deposit and opening of sealed wills (Sec. 42–46), certified copies and encumbrance "
    "certificates (Chapter XX of the Rules), marriage registration, firm and society registration, and cancellation of "
    "registered forged documents by the District Registrar under Sec. 22-C (to be covered in a separate BRD).",
]

